course: dictionary
lesson: 3515
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Fatty is a good example. «Fatty food» and «fatty meat» are about food that contains a lot of fat, and that is the meaning you will meet most in health lessons.
explain: Look at the words around it. «An elephant walks on its tiptoes with a big fatty pad behind the toes» uses fatty to describe something made of fat. The words pad and toes are about a body part, so they point to the meaning made of fat.
explain: Be careful with the third meaning. Calling a person «Fatty» is a rude, insulting name. It hurts people, and it is bullying. When a word is used to hurt someone, do not copy it, and talk to a grown-up if someone uses it on you.
fact: Fatty means containing a lot of fat, like «fatty food» or «fatty meat».
fact: Fatty can also describe something made of fat, like «fatty acids», which are parts of fats.
fact: «Fatty» used as a name for a person is rude and unkind, and it is a form of bullying.
fact: Fatty, heavy food like a big fry-up takes a long time to digest, and it can cause tummy ache and feeling sick.
fact: Some fats are needed for a balanced diet, but fatty foods such as chips, crisps and burgers are best eaten in small amounts.
exercise: What does fatty mean in «fatty food»? | *Containing a lot of fat | Made of metal | Very tall | Freshly cooked
exercise: Maya says «Fatty» is just a joke name for a friend. What does the word really do? | *It is a rude, hurtful name | It is a type of food | It is a kind nickname | It means very fast
exercise: In science, «fatty acids» are parts of fats. What do fatty acids describe? | A kind of weather | A sports game | *Something made of fat | Something that tastes sweet
test: Which meaning fits «a big fatty pad behind the toes»? | *Made of fat | Wet from rain | Very quiet | Cold and icy
test: Why are fatty foods like chips best eaten in small amounts? | They help you run faster | They are always rude | They make you taller | *They are not a big part of a balanced diet
exam: Which sentence uses fatty as an insult? | *«Stop calling him Fatty, it is hurtful.» | «The seed had a fatty bit for the ants.» | «Fatty foods are best in small amounts.» | «The elephant has a big fatty pad.»
